# Seeed XIAO ESP32C5 board configuration
#
# ---- THE ONE LINE THAT DEVIATES FROM UPSTREAM ---------------------------
#
# Upstream selects SOC_ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R8. **That symbol does not exist in
# the Zephyr tree this project pins** (NCS v3.4.0 -> Zephyr 4.4). Ours defines
# exactly one C5 module variant, N8R4, in
# zephyr/soc/espressif/esp32c5/Kconfig.soc — and the board port postdates it.
#
# Adding the symbol upstream-side is not an option: zephyr/ is west-managed and
# gitignored, so a patch there is reverted by the next `west update` without a
# word. Same reasoning as the -Dnrf_crypto_keys_housekeeping() workaround in
# sysbuild/mcuboot_xiao_esp32s3.conf — keep the fix inside this repo.
#
# It is safe to select the N8R4 symbol, and the reason is that the symbol is
# **cosmetic**. Its entire effect in that Kconfig.soc is:
#
#     config SOC_ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R4
#         bool
#         select SOC_ESP32C5
#
#     config SOC_PART_NUMBER
#         default "ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R4" if SOC_ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R4
#
# It selects the SoC and names a string. It drives no memory sizes: flash size
# reaches Kconfig as CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE, computed from the devicetree
# (`dt_node_reg_size_int` in Kconfig.defconfig), and PSRAM size reaches it as
# CONFIG_ESP_SPIRAM_SIZE, computed from the psram0 node's `size` property
# (Kconfig.spiram). Both are devicetree facts, and the .dts sets both to the 8
# MB this board actually carries.
#
# **The one visible consequence** is that `CONFIG_SOC_PART_NUMBER` reads
# "ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R4" on a board fitted with an N8R8. Nothing in this
# firmware reads it. It is wrong in a boot banner and right nowhere, which is
# the cheapest of the available wrongnesses — the alternatives are a patched
# west tree that silently reverts, or a hand-written SoC variant that then has
# to be kept in step with Espressif's.
#
# **When the pinned tree gains SOC_ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R8**, change the select
# below to it and delete the &psram0 override in the .dts. Both, or the board
# ends up with 8 MB of PSRAM declared twice and nobody the wiser.

config BOARD_XIAO_ESP32C5
	select SOC_ESP32_C5_WROOM_1_N8R4
	select SOC_ESP32C5_HPCORE if BOARD_XIAO_ESP32C5_ESP32C5_HPCORE
	select SOC_ESP32C5_LPCORE if BOARD_XIAO_ESP32C5_ESP32C5_LPCORE
